        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{e^{2}}^{e^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$  gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e^{2}$ | $e^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{e^{2}}^{e^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{16}{5}\\int_{e^{2}}^{e^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{16}{5}\\int_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(8\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}}\\right)|_{2}^{4} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(4\\cdot {u}^{2}\\right)|_{2}^{4} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(4\\cdot (16-4)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(48\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
